.TH CTF-HUNTER-ENABLE-CAPTURE 8 "October 2026" "CTF Hunter 0.1.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
ctf-hunter-enable-capture \- authorize terminal capture for one desktop account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkexec /usr/libexec/ctf-hunter-enable-capture
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctf-hunter-enable-capture
is the fixed-purpose administrative helper used by the CTF Hunter desktop
application. It adds the account identified by
.B PKEXEC_UID
to the
.B ctf-hunter
system group after PolicyKit administrator authorization.
.PP
The helper accepts no command-line arguments, rejects direct unprivileged use,
does not infer an account from
.B SUDO_USER
and performs no service or filesystem changes. A new login session is required
before the supplementary group membership becomes active.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PKEXEC_UID
Numeric UID supplied by
.BR pkexec (1).
Root and malformed values are rejected.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/sysusers.d/ctf-hunter.conf
Declarative definition of the
.B ctf-hunter
system group.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/dev.ctfhunter.enable-capture.policy
PolicyKit action restricting execution to this installed helper.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ctf-hunter (1),
.BR ctf-hunter-capture (8),
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR usermod (8)
